# What must never reach a published image.
#
# The first two entries are the ones that matter `[P1-23]`. A developer's `.data/apim.sqlite` holds
# every subscription key and every certificate private key this repository has ever minted, all
# encrypted with the KEK — and `.data/kek.key` sits beside it. Copying the build context wholesale
# into an image publishes both, and nothing about the resulting image looks wrong.
.data/
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-*
*.key
.env
.env.*
.secrets/

# Build outputs and dependencies: reinstalled and rebuilt inside the image, and a host
# `node_modules` may hold platform binaries for the wrong architecture.
node_modules/
ui/node_modules/
ui/dist/

# History and tooling that has no runtime role.
.git/
.github/
.gitignore
reports/
test/
ui/test/
tools/
# The vendored reference portal — a different application, kept as a design reference. It carries
# its own dependencies, its own build cache and its own licence, and none of it runs here.
existing-portal-example/
*.log

# `scripts/` is deliberately absent from this list: `scripts/mint-instance.ts` runs inside the
# control-plane image, because a deployment with no browser still has to enrol a gateway.
